I break from tradition here.  I always use the whip until I can find
something else - usually an elven broadsword or a dwarven short sword
or a silver saber or a unihorn.  However, I never spend the skill
points to advance Whip, because Arcs can advance so many spell classes,
not to mention eventually you'll probably want to go to Expert in Saber
and then Two-weapon.

In general I have found Arcs to be one of the easiest classes to
ascend.  This applies doubly to Gnome Arcs, who can waltz through the
mines letting their pet kill all the gnomes and dwarves and then
scavenging their armor.

